# Drafted by Gemini (R24 wood), edited.

~ edge_start
if not flag.wytchwood_open
-> early
endif
Narrator: The blue-black pines lean at crooked angles, swallowing all sound beyond a few paces while thin shafts of silver moonlight catch hundreds of bone and twig idols clicking overhead.
set ct_wood_entered
set party_size = 1
if flag.tarot_hero_2
set party_size = 2
endif
if flag.tarot_hero_3
set party_size = 3
endif
if flag.tarot_hero_4
set party_size = 4
endif
if days_since.ct_clock >= 4
set horned_bedlam_nights = 4
quest chaos_reigns bedlam
elif days_since.ct_clock >= 3
set horned_bedlam_nights = 3
elif days_since.ct_clock >= 2
set horned_bedlam_nights = 2
elif days_since.ct_clock >= 1
set horned_bedlam_nights = 1
endif
quest the_crooked_tree into_the_wytchwood
-> END

~ early
Narrator: A thick glamour hangs between the trunks, and every path you take bends gently back to the moorland edge.
-> END

~ track_1
Narrator: Here at the forest's threshold, Phillip's trail is little more than a rumour in the damp pine needles.
* [Survival DC 13] Read the ground -> track_1_ok | track_1_fail
* [Nature DC 13] Read the moss and the bark -> track_1_ok | track_1_fail
* [if flag.ct_clue_1] [Survival DC 13 adv] Follow the pocket watch's trail -> track_1_ok | track_1_fail
* Leave -> END

~ track_1_ok
Narrator: You find the subtle press of a gentleman's boot heel leading deeper into the gloom, toward the scent of cold water.
set ct_leg_1_done
-> END

~ track_1_fail
time +60
set ct_fail_1 += 1
if flag.ct_fail_1 >= 2
-> track_1_found
endif
Narrator: An hour slips away in false turns and tangled roots before the clicking overhead stops, and something hungry steps out of the dark.
combat ct_hw_1

~ track_1_found
Narrator: Though the woods have spun you round, a freshly snapped bough finally gives the way away, pointing toward the black creek.
set ct_leg_1_done
-> END

~ track_2
Narrator: On the north bank of the black water, the mud gives way to stone and root, and the way forward grows faint again.
* [Survival DC 13] Read the ground -> track_2_ok | track_2_fail
* [Nature DC 13] Read the moss and the bark -> track_2_ok | track_2_fail
* [if flag.ct_clue_2] [Survival DC 13 adv] Follow the torn cuff's trail -> track_2_ok | track_2_fail
* Leave -> END

~ track_2_ok
Narrator: Scuffed lichen on a low root marks where a staggering man hauled himself up the bank toward the briar thicket.
set ct_leg_2_done
-> END

~ track_2_fail
time +60
set ct_fail_2 += 1
if flag.ct_fail_2 >= 2
-> track_2_found
endif
Narrator: An hour goes by in the freezing damp, and the shadows between the leaning pines begin to crowd in with teeth bared.
combat ct_hw_2

~ track_2_found
Narrator: At last, a smear of creek silt on a pale stone shows where Phillip dragged his feet northward.
set ct_leg_2_done
-> END

~ track_3
Narrator: Past the beast's thicket, the briars thin into a silent hollow where the needles lie undisturbed.
* [Survival DC 13] Read the ground -> track_3_ok | track_3_fail
* [Nature DC 13] Read the moss and the bark -> track_3_ok | track_3_fail
* [if flag.ct_clue_3] [Survival DC 13 adv] Follow the bloodied thorns -> track_3_ok | track_3_fail
* Leave -> END

~ track_3_ok
Narrator: Crushed nightshade stems and a staggered stride lead through the hollow toward a sagging roof in the clearing ahead.
set ct_leg_3_done
-> END

~ track_3_fail
time +60
set ct_fail_3 += 1
if flag.ct_fail_3 >= 2
-> track_3_found
endif
Narrator: You lose a cold hour circling the same bone totems until the branches overhead rustle and the wood's creatures close in.
combat ct_hw_3

~ track_3_found
Narrator: Weariness nearly takes your eyes, yet a line of bruised fern fronds reveals the path Phillip took through the gloom.
set ct_leg_3_done
-> END

~ track_4
Narrator: North of the slanted hovel, the mist curls low over the roots, hiding the way into the deeper grove.
* [Survival DC 13] Read the ground -> track_4_ok | track_4_fail
* [Nature DC 13] Read the moss and the bark -> track_4_ok | track_4_fail
* [if flag.ct_clue_4] [Survival DC 13 adv] Follow the spilled ash -> track_4_ok | track_4_fail
* Leave -> END

~ track_4_ok
Narrator: The trail cuts straight through the pale mist, the footprints deep and unhurried now, drawn toward a whispering grove.
set ct_leg_4_done
quest the_crooked_tree tracking_phillip
-> END

~ track_4_fail
time +60
set ct_fail_4 += 1
if flag.ct_fail_4 >= 2
-> track_4_found
endif
Narrator: An hour drains away in the winding fog before low shapes detach themselves from the timber and lunge.
combat ct_hw_4

~ track_4_found
Narrator: The fog parts around a trail of crushed toadstools, marking Phillip's steady march into the grove ahead.
set ct_leg_4_done
quest the_crooked_tree tracking_phillip
-> END

~ clue_1
Narrator: Something catches the thin silver moonlight beneath a mat of damp blue-black pine needles.
* [Investigation DC 13] Search the needles -> clue_1_ok | clue_1_f
* [Perception DC 13] Look more carefully -> clue_1_ok | clue_1_f
* Leave -> END

~ clue_1_ok
give clue_pocket_watch
set ct_clue_1
Narrator: You brush the cold needles aside and lift a heavy silver pocket watch, its case engraved with the initials P.D. and its crystal cracked across the midnight hour.
-> END

~ clue_1_f
Narrator: Your fingers find only wet pine needles, brittle twigs, and cold black soil.
-> clue_1

~ clue_2
Narrator: The smell of spilled lamp oil lingers near the crooked roots beside the trail.
* [Investigation DC 13] Search the roots -> clue_2_ok | clue_2_f
* [Perception DC 13] Look more carefully -> clue_2_ok | clue_2_f
* Leave -> END

~ clue_2_ok
give clue_lantern
set ct_clue_2
Narrator: Wedged between two black roots lies a fine brass hooded lantern, its glass pane shattered and its wick still damp with oil.
-> END

~ clue_2_f
Narrator: The shadows beneath the twisted roots yield only dead moss and smooth dark stones.
-> clue_2

~ clue_3
Narrator: A faint trace of harsh spirits cuts through the cold scent of pine sap and rot.
* [Investigation DC 13] Search the brush -> clue_3_ok | clue_3_f
* [Perception DC 13] Look more carefully -> clue_3_ok | clue_3_f
* Leave -> END

~ clue_3_ok
give clue_hip_flask
set ct_clue_3
Narrator: Half-buried in the ferns is a dented silver hip flask engraved with the letters P.D., its stopper missing and its last drops soaked into the moss.
-> END

~ clue_3_f
Narrator: You part the cold ferns, but find nothing among the tangled stems.
-> clue_3

~ clue_4
Narrator: The low briars beside the path have been snapped and trampled by a heavy stride.
* [Investigation DC 13] Search the briars -> clue_4_ok | clue_4_f
* [Perception DC 13] Look more carefully -> clue_4_ok | clue_4_f
* Leave -> END

~ clue_4_ok
give clue_cloth
set ct_clue_4
Narrator: Caught on a long black thorn is a torn scrap of fine pinstriped wool from Lord Phillip's coat, stiff with dried mud.
-> END

~ clue_4_f
Narrator: The thorns catch at your sleeves, offering only dead leaves and old cobwebs.
-> clue_4

~ clue_5
give clue_cane
set ct_clue_5
if flag.tarot_hero_1 == "the_devil" or flag.tarot_hero_2 == "the_devil" or flag.tarot_hero_3 == "the_devil" or flag.tarot_hero_4 == "the_devil"
give phillips_cane
endif
Narrator: Laid neatly across the narrow goat path is Phillip's ebony walking stick, its silver goat head cold as river stone, left behind by a man who no longer needed to lean.
-> END

~ creek
if flag.ct_hw_swept_done and not flag.ct_creek_crossed
-> creek_rejoin
endif
Narrator: Black water forty feet across rushes past too quick for the pitch of the land, chattering over its stones like a sack of dry bones. A slick pine trunk spans the froth, a crooked line of wet boulders breaks the current, and a gravel bar offers a chest-deep ford.
* [Athletics DC 13] Walk the fallen log. -> creek_ok | creek_swept
* [Acrobatics DC 13] Cross by the wet stones. -> creek_ok | creek_swept
* [Survival DC 13] Wade the gravel ford. -> creek_ok | creek_swept
* Turn back from the bank. -> END

~ creek_ok
Narrator: You gain the north bank with boots full of ice-cold water and pine needles clinging to your hems, the roar of the creek dying behind you after three strides.
set ct_creek_crossed
quest the_crooked_tree tracking_phillip
move ct_wytchwood:north_bank
-> END

~ creek_swept
Narrator: The black current takes {name} off their feet in a breath, dragging them downstream into the dark while the rest of you scramble along the roots to catch up. When you haul {name} coughing onto the mud, the root-tangle along the bank begins to uncoil.
combat ct_hw_swept

~ creek_rejoin
Narrator: With the bank quiet again, you haul {name} up out of the black silt, link arms against the pull of the water, and cross together to the northern side.
set ct_creek_crossed
quest the_crooked_tree tracking_phillip
move ct_wytchwood:north_bank
-> END

~ heart_start
Narrator: Ahead, the leaning pines thin around a low rise, and a warm amber glow flickers between the trunks like a campfire waiting at the end of a long road.
set ct_heart_reached
quest the_crooked_tree six_horns_his_crown
-> END
